<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African issues flood warnings after heavy rains.</title>
<headline>S.African issues flood warnings after heavy rains.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Department of Water and Forestry on Thursday issued a flood warning to residents downstream of the Vaal and Bloemhof dams following a &quot;dramatic&quot; increase in water levels.</p>
<p>Water levels in the Vaal Dam have reached 119 percent of design capacity while the Bloemhof dam is 111 percent full, following recent heavy and unseasonal rains.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
